      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DIS IS HEAVEN (1) sets the standard on exposed grade, resuming off a Benchmark 82 win at Inverell over 1200m, where he finished strongly and scored by a neck, with a close Tuncurry trial adding readiness. The 64kg and drop back to 1000m are the balancing points, but his distance record is strong. WHERE'S THE FIRE (2) is the main danger after a Benchmark 74 fourth at Tuncurry, beaten just over a length despite first-turn tightening, and the claim gives him a kinder weight. BRAZEN BRANDO (5) has a place-to-win bridge to cross, yet his last-start Taree run had interference and the inside draw gives him a cleaner chance to produce his best. BLUE DANE (3) is harder to trust after two plain runs before the spell, including a heavy-track Class 2 collapse, but first-up conditions, blinkers and repeated 1000m placings leave her as the value runner of the selected quartet.",
